      "hints": [
        "Substitute $\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta$ into $3\\cos^4\\theta + 4\\sin^2\\theta - 3 = 0$.",
        "Replace $\\cos^2\\theta = x$ to obtain $3x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the identity $\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta$ in the given equation:\n$$3\\cos^4\\theta + 4(1 - \\cos^2\\theta) - 3 = 0$$",
        "Let $x = \\cos^2\\theta$:\n$$3x^2 + 4(1 - x) - 3 = 0 \\implies 3x^2 - 4x + 4 - 3 = 0 \\implies 3x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0$$"
